 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Ghosting Artifacts:** Pixel-aligned methods generate redundant and inconsistent primitives in overlapping regions, leading to ghosting. This method addresses this by using a global volume and filtering duplicates [S2].
-*   **Depth Noise:** Monocular depth predictions contain noise and floating artifacts. This method handles this by applying a statistical filter to remove floaters after uniform filtering [S2].
-*   **Recursive Convergence:** The position offset $\Delta \mu_i$ depends on the previous estimation. The sources note that $\Delta \mu_i$ is stabilized to a stationary point at infinite training iterations. During inference, two recursive iterations are empirically sufficient for convergence [S2].
